ressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAMEOKA AKIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOSUGE MASAHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KUDO TAKAFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAMEOKA, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOSUGE, MASAHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUDO, TAKAFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A thermoplastic resin composition containing inorganic particles, characterized in that (i) the inorganic particles have a void volume of 0.1 to 3 ml/g and (ii) the surface of the inorganic particles has been treated with a water-compatible polyester or an organosilicon compound in an amount of 0.05 to 10 times by weight the amount of the particles. The composition can be obtained by feeding a dispersion of the surface-treated inorganic particles to a vented twin-screw kneading extruder to mix the dispersion with a thermoplastic resin.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Composition de résine thermoplastique contenant des particules inorganiques, caractérisée en ce que (i) les particules inorganiques ont un volume vide de 0,1 à 3 ml/g, et (ii) la surface des particules inorganiques a été traitée par un polyester compatible à l'eau ou un composé organosilicique en une quantité de 0,05 à 10 fois, en poids, la quantité des particules. La composition peut être obtenue en chargeant une dispersion de particules inorganiques traitées en surface dans un malaxeur-extrudeur, à évacuation des gaz, à double vis sans fin, en vue de mélanger la dispersion avec une résine thermoplastique.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>